# ── ICE fetch state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# stock_report_hits.json is NOT here on purpose. It is the dated publish-time
# log — one entry per date — and it is the learned state behind tiers 0 and 1.
# 619 commits its copy; 620 commits this one. Both repos run the same fetcher
# and must learn the same way, so an ignored (and therefore per-run, throwaway)
# copy here would mean 620 relearning from zero on every run and searching in a
# different order from 619 — which is exactly what the shadow comparison is
# supposed to be measuring against. The dated history is not sensitive: ICE
# publishes these reports publicly and the log records only when it did so.
#
# These stay uncommitted. They are per-run, not learned:
#
#   stock_report_cursor.json  where an interrupted sweep got to, plus the list
#                             of dates tier 1 has already been spent on. Both
#                             are meaningful only within a run's own lifetime.
#   ice_run_stats.json        per-run request/throttle diagnostics. Uploaded as
#                             a workflow artifact instead, where it is kept for
#                             30 days without accreting into git history.
#   state/ice_block_state.json  edge-triggered block notification state.
fetch/scraper/sources/ice_certified_stocks/stock_report_cursor.json
fetch/scraper/sources/ice_certified_stocks/ice_run_stats.json
fetch/state/
_stage/
